.TH SIGMA_DIFFERENCE 1 2000-1月 "codon.bias_B.FC" "codon.bias_B.FC"
.SH NAME
codon.bias_B.FC \- The \fBB(F|C)\fR codon usage bias difference between two gene classes (the
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIcodon.bias_B.FC(\fBf\fR as <generic> CodonUsageProfile, 
\fBc\fR as <generic> CodonUsageProfile);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBB(F|C)\fR codon usage bias difference between two gene classes (the
 paper's formula [1]):

\fB
 B(F|C) = SUM_a p_a(F) SUM_{(x,y,z)->a} | f(x,y,z) - c(x,y,z) |
 \fR`

 the per-codon absolute difference weighted by the amino acid frequency of
 the query class F. Note that this measurement is asymmetric: F is the
 query object and C is the reference ruler.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBf\fB \fR\- the query codon usage profile (gene family F). 
.PP
.PP
\fBc\fB \fR\- the reference codon usage profile (class C). 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the B(F|C) value
.PP
